If we don't have an server to practice, We can use container as an server.

1. Create an container with ubuntu image
"docker run -d --name server1 ubuntu:24.04 sleep infinity"

2. Verify the container
"docker ps"

3. Enter the container
"docker exec -it server1 bash"

4. Update and install the required packages
"apt update"
"apt install -y openssh-server"
"apt install -y python3"

5. Create runtime directory
" mkdir -p /run/sshd"

6. Start ssh manually
"/usr/sbin/sshd"

7. Verify ssh is running
""ps aux | grep '[s]shd'"

8. create user and set password

9. Install sudo
"apt install -y sudo"

10. Add user to sudo grp

11. Return back to your machine and find  ip of the container
"docker inspect -f '{{range.NetworkSettings.Networks}}{{.IPAddress}}{{end}}' server1"
